\[
p_{1}x_{1}+p_{2}x_{2}=w
\]

\end_inset

The Lagrangian of this problem is
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
L=x_{1}^{\alpha}x_{2}^{1-\alpha}+\lambda(w-p_{1}x_{1}-p_{2}x_{2})
\]

\end_inset

and the first-order conditions are
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{1}}=0\iff\alpha x_{1}^{\alpha-1}x_{2}^{1-\alpha}=\lambda p_{1}\\
\frac{\partial L}{\partial x_{2}}=0\iff(1-\alpha)x_{1}^{\alpha}x_{2}^{-\alpha}=\lambda p_{2}
\end{gather*}

\end_inset

Equating the two equations we have
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\lambda=\frac{\alpha x_{1}^{\alpha-1}x_{2}^{1-\alpha}}{p_{1}}=\frac{(1-\alpha)x_{1}^{\alpha}x_{2}^{-\alpha}}{p_{2}}
\]

\end_inset

and solving for 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{2}$
\end_inset

