\end_inset

?
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Proof
Part A of this problem will be skipped.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof

\bar under
Part B.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since the agent prefers bundles with more 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}$
\end_inset

 to all other bundles, the agent maximizes his utility on 
\begin_inset Formula $B(p,w)$
\end_inset

 by consuming as much 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}$
\end_inset

 as possible.
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
x_{1}^{lex}(p,w)=\frac{w}{p_{1}}\\
x_{2}^{lex}(p,w)=0
\end{gather*}

\end_inset


\bar under
Part C.
\bar default

\begin_inset Formula 
\[
S_{lk}(p,w)=\frac{\partial x_{l}(p,w)}{\partial p_{k}}+\frac{\partial x_{l}(p,w)}{\partial w}x_{k}(p,w)
\]

\end_inset

The value of the Slutsky matrix associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{\succsim}$
\end_inset

 at some arbitrary 
\begin_inset Formula $p\in\mathbb{R}_{++}^{2}$
\end_inset

 and 
